WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.874
Meet Switchboard.

2
00:00:01.874 --> 00:00:03.201
The same website.

3
00:00:03.201 --> 00:00:07.015
A more manageable next step, using a single switch.

4
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.704
A form is more than a collection of boxes.

5
00:00:12.704 --> 00:00:18.760
You need to find controls, enter information, understand errors, and recover your place.

6
00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.304
Limited input makes that whole journey important.

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:30.144
The installed extension reads the real form and organizes its controls into sections.

8
00:00:30.144 --> 00:00:32.232
The website stays in charge.

9
00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:37.064
Switchboard provides a structured view, not a disconnected imitation.

10
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.580
Start scanning, and the blue focus moves automatically.

11
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.892
Press Space to choose a section, then a field.

12
00:00:45.892 --> 00:00:49.474
A switch mapped to Space follows the same input path.

13
00:00:49.474 --> 00:00:53.637
Scan waits are condensed here; this is not a speed benchmark.

14
00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.129
Text entry uses a row and character keyboard.

15
00:01:00.129 --> 00:01:04.588
Choose a row, choose a letter, and repeat with the same switch.

16
00:01:04.588 --> 00:01:08.222
Here, both the name and email are entered through that path.

17
00:01:08.222 --> 00:01:11.430
Each applied character updates the original page.

18
00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.201
Nothing is being pasted into a separate mockup.

19
00:01:14.201 --> 00:01:16.521
You can pause scanning whenever you need to.

20
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:28.178
The same approach handles workshop options, radio buttons, and checkboxes.

21
00:01:28.178 --> 00:01:32.392
Once the required fields are ready, review the actual values.

22
00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:35.021
This screen does not submit anything.

23
00:01:35.021 --> 00:01:38.500
The final action still needs your explicit confirmation.

24
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:45.861
Now the website rejects our request: the laser-cutting workshop is full.

25
00:01:45.861 --> 00:01:48.140
That response comes from the practice server.

26
00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:55.592
Switchboard reads the website's error and marks the section that needs attention, instead of pretending
the task succeeded.

27
00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.129
Return to the marked section and choose a different workshop.

28
00:02:00.129 --> 00:02:04.304
The correction updates the real page, and its error clears.

29
00:02:04.304 --> 00:02:06.276
Review again before sending.

30
00:02:06.276 --> 00:02:10.863
If the form changes after a review, Switchboard requires a fresh one.

31
00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:16.114
Confirm, and the website returns a practice receipt.

32
00:02:16.114 --> 00:02:20.642
Switchboard quotes its response, rather than inventing success.

33
00:02:20.642 --> 00:02:25.573
This event is fictional; the submission and server validation are real.

34
00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:31.894
Processing stays local, with no AI service or saved form history.

35
00:02:31.894 --> 00:02:34.188
Access is user activated.

36
00:02:34.188 --> 00:02:39.034
Websites still control their own data handling, including autosave.

37
00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:45.018
Tests cover the complete one-switch workflow and installed extension.

38
00:02:45.018 --> 00:02:46.642
Native forms only.

39
00:02:46.642 --> 00:02:49.258
Hardware and user testing come next.

40
00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:53.529
Switchboard.

41
00:02:53.529 --> 00:02:58.323
A clearer path through, with the next action always yours to choose.
